now that morbius is a movie star you  might find yourself wondering just who  is this classic marvel foe you may know  his spider-man connection but what about  his bond with she-hulk here's everything  you need to know about morbius the  living vampire  nowadays in marvel comics morbius often  walks the line between a good guy and a  bad guy if you're getting mugged and the  living vampire happens to walk by he'll  probably step in and help but he's also  likely to get himself a snack at the  same time when he first showed up in  1971's amazing spider-man number 101  however there was no anti-hero nonsense  going on morbius was a stone-cold killer  amazing spider-man number 101 was  memorable for a few reasons most notably  it was the first issue of the comic that  wasn't written by stan lee roy thomas  took over writing duties and lee had  left thomas with a bit of a cliffhanger  peter parker had suddenly found himself  with six arms so in this comic  spider-man seeks out the nobel  prize-winning dr morbius hoping that he  can find a cure in the doctor's research  instead he finds a blood-sucking vampire  with a mean streak both thomas and jerry  conway who wrote morbius's subsequent  appearances in marvel team-up told back  issue in 2009 that they never imagined  morbius would go on to become a dark  hero conway said i more or less thought  of him as a one-shot villain they both  agree though that the foundation for  something more was there in morbius's  first appearance conway said both sides  of him were always there he was always  supposed to be a fairly sympathetic  character  some fans believe that morbius was  rendered a living vampire as a sneaky  way of getting around the comics code  and that his subsequent popularity  helped force changes to the code itself  the comics code was a self-imposed  industry standard that among other  things banned any depictions of the  undead morbius's living status was  marvel's loophole or so the legend told  the truth is that morbius's creation was  actually a response to the comics code  loosening of its rules about vampire  zombies and other undead creatures at  the same time stan lee wanted to  capitalize on the code's newer more  liberal attitude roy thomas has said  that he and lee first discussed using  dracula as the villain in amazing  spider-man number 101  children of the night  what music they need but lee wanted a  costumed villain instead ironically  while morbius didn't create any friction  with the comics code years later another  artist claimed to have locked horns with  the code over his work on the character  penciller ron wagner worked on the first  14 issues of morbius the living vampire  and apparently got in a heap of trouble  for his use of sexually explicit  drawings in the comic  while morbius's living status was not a  sneaky way around the comics code it was  an important aspect of his character for  one thing it allowed him to remain in  the marvel universe for longer than his  undead contemporaries in 1983's dr  strange number 62 the sorcerer supreme  uses his magic to boost the montessie  formula killing marvel's version of  dracula and the rest of the world's  vampires eventually dracula would return  in the series night stalkers but that  comeback was a whole decade in the  making and in the meantime one vampire  remained completely unaffected by any of  it morbius because morbius's condition  has nothing to do with traditional  vampirism doctor strange's war on  dracula has no impact on dr morbius  beyond freeing up the playing field from  competition anyway  according to morbius co-creator roy  thomas the conception of the living  vampire involved a marriage of various  campy science fiction references though  not all of them were intentional  morbius's name came from the character  dr edward morbius from the 1956 film  forbidden planet apparently though this  wasn't a conscious choice and thomas  didn't realize that that's where he had  lifted the name from until after the  comic was already on the racks thomas  has also revealed that the inspiration  for morbius's origin as a creature of  science fiction rather than fantasy came  from a film he had seen in his youth one  in which radiation not magic turned a  character into a vampire during his  interview with back issue however he  could not remember the film's name while  neither film fits exactly with thomas's  memory two films released in 1957 just a  year after forbidden planet could fit  the bill of science created vampires not  of this earth features an alien who  disguises himself as human and drains  victims of their blood the same year saw  the release of the vampire about a man  who unwittingly contracts vampirism  after ingesting pills made of vampire  bad blood  one of the most important stories in  morbius's history involves a weird  violent court scene in the pages of  savage she-hulk temporarily cured of his  condition dr morbius is working on ways  to help lawyer jennifer walters better  known as she-hulk from dying  unfortunately for her morbius is due to  stand trial for his many crimes walters  subsequently defends morbius during the  trial and uses a bizarre method to  protect her client to prove morbius was  not in control of his actions while he  was a vampire walters brings a pair of  rabbits into the court and feeds one of  them the formula that transformed him  predictably the rabbit immediately goes  full holy grail and kills its furry  mates  walters succeeds in getting morbius's  charges reduced and the living vampire's  transformation from outright villain to  morally ambiguous anti-hero is complete  the morbius of the ultimate universe was  introduced in ultimate spider-man number  95. this version of morbius is more  connected to the vampires of his world  than his marvel earth prime counterpart  he's a more traditional undead vampire  who even tells spider-man that he is the  son of dracula ironically though more  attached to the world of the undead than  the original the ultimate morbius is not  only not a villain but actually spends  much of his time hunting his vampiric  brethren while marvel officially nailed  the coffin on its ultimate line of  comics in 2015 with the secret wars  tie-in miniseries ultimate end the  ultimate line's impact on marvel's film  adaptations can't be ignored nick fury  was first drawn as samuel jackson in  ultimates six years before the actor  appeared in iron man black widow and  hawkeye being a part of the original  avengers lineup is an ultimate holdover  too as is captain america's world war ii  era outfit and the alien chitari while  the origin of the character in morbius  fits more with the original marvel  version you could argue some aspects are  inspired by the ultimate line including  his more heroic nature and his conflict  with fellow vampire milo  if it had been up to screenwriter and  director david s goyer the living  vampire's first big screen appearance  would likely have predated the mcu by a  half decade at least in a deleted scene  found on the dvd of 1998's blade a  mysterious figure in a dark trench coat  watches from a nearby rooftop as blade  and karen emerge triumphant from their  conflict with lamagra goyer the film's  writer has since confirmed the figure  was morbius and claims that had goyer  gone on to direct blade 2 morbius would  have been the villain for the sequel  instead guillermo del toro directed  blade 2 and the story was altered  jettisoning him all together it would no  doubt be fascinating to sidestep into an  alternate reality where goyer got to  write his version of blade 2. morbius  was a character full of potential for  that series particularly if gwyer meant  to stay true to the tragic and more  sympathetic nature of the character  deacon frost the villain of blade was a  ruthless killer and the villains of  blade 2 weren't much better a more  tortured and conflicted antagonist may  have made for an intriguing contrast  morpheus is far from the only marvel  character based on a classic kind of  monster though it took until 2021 to  reveal a connection between the living  vampire and calvin zabo also known as mr  hyde agents of shield fans may remember  kyle mclaughlin had a recurring role as  cal on season two of the series  [Music]  oh  and there goes the feeling in my legs in  the comics hyde is a genuine powerhouse  able to hold his own against earth's  mightiest heroes in the 2021 one-shot  morbius bond of blood it's revealed that  morbius and zabo have known each other  since before either were transformed  into their more monstrous selves morbius  strikes a deal with zabo in the hopes of  saving a child's life but as you might  predict things don't exactly work out  well more recently a further connection  has been revealed between morbius's  condition and another monstrous marvel  scientist in 2022's amazing spider-man  number 92 kurt connors becomes infected  with the vampire's condition the  development sends conor's on a rampage  and renders him more dangerous than ever  spidey misty knight and colleen wing  then recruit morbius to help him stop  conor's and cure him of his disease  for much of his comic book existence  morbius has walked a morally ambiguous  line he usually fights on the side of  good but he's a lot less picky about the  methods he employs than other heroes but  in 2022 morbius pole vaulted out of the  anti-hero zone into outright villainous  territory in recent years michael  morbius has continued to search for a  cure to his condition when he surfaces  again in 2022's amazing spider-man  number 77 his illness has worsened  sending him on a near mindless rampage  the ben reilly spider-man confronts him  when he finds morbia standing over the  bodies of a half dozen or so victims the  vampire attacks spidey without  provocation and the issue ends with  morbius sinking his teeth into riley's  neck with riley weakened by morbius's  attack it's up to misty knight and  colleen wing to take morbius down in the  following issue unfortunately the beyond  corporation takes the opportunity to  experiment on morbius against his will  on the bright side they stabilized his  condition in the process so that when  he's revived in amazing spider-man  number 92 he's back to his old self  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite comic book characters are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

